%# expected-result: FAIL
%description:
Expected failure by explicit maintainer decision: defer this nontrivial repair to future work.
Repair requires observable production coding selection and separation of capability negotiation from coding support; the current explicit testability assertion must also be replaced.
Evidence and deferred-repair decision: doc/project/evidence/model/wifi/results.md#deferred-repair-expectations.
This declaration records unresolved work, not supported behavior.

Testability gap: No LDPC transmit-code discriminator is exposed by the VHT mode API; this test cannot establish the coding obligation.
The failure is an explicit missing observation, not proof that an emitted frame is wrong.

%file: Ac_Ldpc.cc

#include "ProtocolTest.h"
#include "WifiTestSupport.h"
#include "inet/physicallayer/wireless/ieee80211/mode/Ieee80211VhtMode.h"

namespace inet {
namespace protocoltest {

using namespace inet::physicallayer;

Define_ProtocolTest(wifi_11ac_ldpc)
{
    return ProtocolTest("wifi_11ac_ldpc")
        .once(on("sta1.wlan[0].mac").signal("packetSentToLower")
                  .filterPacket("ieee80211mac.type == 40")
                  .assertEvent([](const MatchContext&) -> bool {
                      throw cRuntimeError("TESTABILITY GAP: No LDPC transmit-code discriminator is exposed by the VHT mode API; this test cannot establish the coding obligation");
                  })
                  .describe("QoS data frame transmitted with LDPC channel coding").within(2.5));
}

} // namespace protocoltest
} // namespace inet

%inifile: test.ini

[General]
*.tester.testName = "wifi_11ac_ldpc"
include ../../ini/_ac.ini
**.wlan[*].radio.receiver.energyDetection = -105dBm
include ../../ini/_base.ini

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST wifi_11ac_ldpc: PASS
